Step 15: Create GitHub Actions workflow
Where: PowerShell

Create the workflow directories:


powershell
mkdir .github
mkdir .github\workflows
Create the workflow file:


powershell
notepad .github\workflows\ci-dockerhub.yml
File 6: ci-dockerhub.yml

Paste:


yaml

name: Python CI DockerHub Pipeline

on:
  push:
    branches:
      - main

jobs:
  build:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest

    steps:
      - name: Checkout repository
        uses: actions/checkout@v4

      - name: Set up Python
        uses: actions/setup-python@v5
        with:
          python-version: '3.12'

      - name: Install dependencies
        run: pip install -r requirements.txt

      - name: Run Pytest
        run: python -m pytest -q

      - name: Set up Docker Buildx
        uses: docker/setup-buildx-action@v3

      - name: Login to Docker Hub
        uses: docker/login-action@v3
        with:
          username: ${{ secrets.DOCKERHUB_USERNAME }}
          password: ${{ secrets.DOCKERHUB_TOKEN }}

      - name: Build and Push Docker Image
        uses: docker/build-push-action@v6
        with:
          context: .
          push: true
          tags: ${{ secrets.DOCKERHUB_USERNAME }}/python-ci-lab:latest
Save and close.

This workflow automatically executes when changes are pushed to the main branch.

Step 16: Create a Docker Hub repository
Where: Docker Hub website

Open:

Docker Hub 
Follow these steps:

Sign in to Docker Hub.

Click Create repository.

Enter repository name: python-ci-lab.

Select Public.

Click Create.

The image will be published using this naming format:


text
YOUR_DOCKERHUB_USERNAME/python-ci-lab:latest
Step 17: Generate Docker Hub access token
Where: Docker Hub website

Open Account Settings.

Go to Personal access tokens.

Click Generate new token.

Enter token description: github-actions.

Select Read & Write permissions.

Generate the token.

Copy and save it securely.

Do not share this token publicly.

Step 18: Add GitHub repository secrets
Where: GitHub website

Open your repository settings:

GitHub Actions Secrets 
Click New repository secret.

Create two secrets:

Secret name

Value

DOCKERHUB_USERNAME

Your Docker Hub username

DOCKERHUB_TOKEN

Your Docker Hub access token

Save both secrets.

These secrets allow GitHub Actions to authenticate with Docker Hub securely.

